.UPDATE...
Issued at 911 AM PDT Sat Jul 25 2026

Stratus had a difficult time developing overnight into early this
morning, despite a marine layer of around 900 feet per the 12Z
OAK upper air sounding. That said, very shallow fog was observed
in the Russian River Valley (which has since dissipated) and
stratus was observed via satellite along the San Mateo coastline,
into the western hills of the East Bay, and around the Monterey
Bay region. Currently satellite imagery is showing lingering
stratus along the San Mateo coastline. With the lack of cloud
cover, temperatures this afternoon may be a few degrees warmer
than what is currently forecast. However, onshore winds will
persist throughout the day and allow for the marine influences to
still be there.

