.SHORT TERM...
Issued at 1222 AM PDT Sat Jul 25 2026
(Today and tonight)

Persistence forecast with very little change in ambient weather
conditions from 24hrs ago and no guidance indicating that the
remainder of tonight and tomorrow will unfold much different than
what we saw today. Dry air just above the marine layer continues to
disrupt the inland intrusion we normally see this time of year, but
not prevent it entirely, as persistent troughing over the EPAC and
the western flank of high pressure centered over the Four Corners
region continue to intersect over the Bay Area and Central Coast.
The most impactful concern is the Beach Hazards Statement that goes
into effect later this morning. Long period southerly swell from
distant Fausto will make for dangerous sneaker waves and riptides.
Never turn your back on the ocean and swim near lifeguards this
weekend.

