.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1222 AM PDT Sat Jul 25 2026
(Sunday through Friday)

Normal temperatures for this time of year will continue through the
weekend into the first half of next week, with very little change
day-to-day through the middle of the week. Interior temperatures
begin to rise a little more by the second half of the week as the
area of high pressure expands westward and Fausto helps to push
the persistent trough north and we begin to see H50 height rises
over the EPAC. We begin to see more widespread Moderate HeatRisk
across the interior by the end of the week into next weekend.

