.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 425 AM PDT Sat Jul 25 2026

Surprise! All terminals are VFR this morning. Honestly we did not
expect that to happen, so what did we miss? Buoy observations
reveal that the dew point has dropped below the sea surface
temperature. That makes it very hard to saturation to occur as the
air temp struggles to get any colder than the ocean. So dry air
has mixed in to the boundary layer, lowering the dew point and
clearing out the clouds. The 12Z weather balloon found a 900 ft
unsaturated marine layer with much warmer and drier air aloft. It
looks like this dry air will be with us all day, so enjoy the
clear skies, aviators!

Vicinity of SFO...It`s unusual to see the cloud coverage decrease
at this hour, but that`s been the trend for the last several
hours as the dry air infiltrates the shallow marine layer. Winds
will remain steady all day from the typical westerly direction.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...There is a small patch of stratus north
of SNS, but it hasn`t shown much ambition. VFR conditions will
likely prevail through the day with the standard diurnally driven
wind regime at both MRY and SNS.

